// Projectiles: what flies (or beams) once something fires or throws it.
// `class` says how it moves and what touching something does:
//   straight  flies in a line (with `gravity` it drops); bursts into its
//             `blast` on contact, or hits for `damage` and is gone;
//   shell     arcs and bounces until it has flown `arm` seconds, then
//             bursts on the next contact (or when its life runs out);
//   thrown    bounces dully and comes to rest; bursts when its life runs
//             out, or, with a `trigger`, when an enemy comes near (a mine);
//   beam      an instant line from the eye: `damage` at up to `range`.
// Anything that fires one names it: weapons, turrets, throwables.
{
  // A blue disc with a light blue ribbon behind it.
  "disc": { "model": "disc", "color": [0.12, 0.42, 1.0],
    "trail": { "style": "ribbon", "color": [0.55, 0.85, 1.0] },
